      "claim": "Sematilide, a benzamide analogue, has an absolute oral bioavailability of 0.46 ± 0.13 from plasma data, still well above the 20% threshold, supporting high F for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C33"],
      "claim": "Loperamide has very low absolute oral bioavailability (0.3%) attributed to P-gp efflux and low solubility, but its large lipophilic structure and transporter liability are not shared by the small polar benzamide query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
